d have kept the top-left under White's control. The 20k took C8 on the next move, the engine's own choice."}, {"turn": 18, "text": "White's F2 lost 4.7 points, with the lead going from +4.1 to +8.8 for Black. The engine's choice was F3, the point the 20k then took, so Black got a useful move at the bottom."}, {"turn": 22, "text": "The decisive move. C6 lost 9.0 points, GPT-6.1 Sol's worst of the game, and pushed Black's lead from +4.5 to +13.4. The engine preferred B6, which Black then took. After that the left side stayed White's but the game was no longer close, and the 20k's best later move was still a 3.5-point loss at B6."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "Everything it ran works on the current position or on records: current-position-liberties.js (inspectLiberties) only parses the board text and lists chains with their distinct liberties, the regions function counts empty regions and their bordering colours, and the rest was reading and writing game notes, SGF and AGENTS.md. Nothing loops over candidate moves, scores points or plays a sequence forward, so every move was chosen by the player.", "stop": false}}